    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0443" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/1–552: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the United States Delegation to
                        the General Assembly</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Roosevelt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1952-01-05T22:00:00+01:00">January 5, 1952—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Delga 879. Re Ital membership in GA. Belaunde told Gross that he had met De
                    Gasperi and discussed tactics re Italy’s admission to UN. Belaunde reported that
                    De Gasperi had asked him not to press his plan but to let things proceed for a
                    while as they are. Belaunde seemed undetermined exactly how to handle his item
                    when it is reached. We will keep in close touch with him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
